Since \( x \) and \( y \) are positive integers, the equation must hold for all \( x \) and \( y \). The only way this can happen is if the coefficients of \( x \) and \( y \) are zero:
1. \( 3n - 12 = 0 \)
2. \( 2n - 12 = 0 \)

